// `[-x]` with an Int `x` is a `[Int]`, which isn't the `[Any]` the
// first `f` takes, so `f(1)` would need `f` for `[Int]`, then for
// `[[Int]]`, without end. Another overload taking the call only
// keeps the error from being reported in the body.
// expect-error: `f` calls itself with types bigger than the ones it was given
fn f(xs: [Any]) => 42;
fn f(x) => f([-x]);
print(f(1));
